```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%User{id: 1, name: "Leanne Graham"}
```

## Loading many at once

`load_many/2` is what keeps an association over a list from querying once per record. It returns a `{record, records}` pair per record, in the order they were given, always with a list on the right. Records looking for the same thing are searched for once, so three users cost one request between them.

```elixir
Blog.load_many([%User{id: 1}, %User{id: 2}, %User{id: 3}], :posts)
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```

