## Association paths

A path walks one association of the records the one before it found, the way `get_in/2` walks a nested map. Every hop is searched for in its own batch, no matter how many records reached it, so the two logged lines are the whole cost of reading every comment on every post a user wrote.

```elixir
Blog.load(user, [:posts, :comments])
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```

