## Running the searches in turn

The searches of a single hop run concurrently, each in its own task. Where `list/3` has to run in the process asking for it, such as inside an `Ecto.Repo` transaction, which is bound to the process that opened it, `async: false` makes the calls in turn instead.

```elixir
Blog.load_many(posts, :comments, async: false)
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```

13:49:18.662 [info] list Comment by [:post_id] for 10 rows
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

